# MSBuild reads this for every build, restore, test and publish of a project under this
# directory (dotnet build/restore/test/publish included).
#
# The shared RedBamboo.AppHost (../redbamboo-packages) multi-targets net9.0 and
# net9.0-windows. Off Windows, NuGet restore refuses the Windows target framework unless
# Windows targeting is enabled, even though the Linux host only builds and uses AppHost's
# net9.0 flavour. Restore walks project references with global properties only (it ignores
# ProjectReference AdditionalProperties), so this cannot be scoped to that one reference
# from here. On Windows the property has no effect. Same mechanism as RedLeaf.
-p:EnableWindowsTargeting=true
